GD6100 is high-precision instrument for testing dielectric loss angle and volume resistivity of insulating oil or other insulating liquids.
When using it, everyone should pay attention to using clean compressed air and oxygen to purge the core of the equipment, the surface and gap of the fixture to effectively remove foreign objects in the equipment. In addition, the user should also pay attention to carefully check the fixtures, tightening bolts, fixing bolts and inner screws for looseness.
The user should pay attention to regularly check whether the lead of the weather-resistant dry-type transformer is intact, whether there is any deformation, brittleness, and lead-free lines. In addition, the user should pay attention to test the dry transformer leads and overheated joints, and whether the lead connector is reliable.
