U.K. grocery giant Tesco answered that question in part last week when it announced acommercial partnershipwith Germany-based Gorillas. Under the pilot program, Tesco will co-locate Gorillas micro-warehouses at several of its stores in the London area, offering a limited assortment for delivery by Gorillas to shoppers’ in 10 minutes or less.
Ultrafast startups that deliver goods from tiny warehouses to shoppers in population-dense markets in 15 minutes or less have zoomed across Europe and generated significant buzz throughout the continent. In the U.S., these firms are just starting to get acclimated, with the majority currently duking it out in New York City.
