Outdoor advertising has been, historically speaking, one of the most prominent and widespread marketing tactics because of the hefty revenues it has managed to bring to a plethora of businesses. Companies like McDonald’s, Amazon, Google, and Geico spend copious amounts of money on this mode of advertising, which should give readers glaring indications as to its success.
In this present writing, we’ll be explaining what an LED billboard truck is, how it works, why you should invest in it, and its pricing (for both rental and purchase).
A digital billboard truck or “mobile billboard”, as its name might suggest, is a vehicle equipped with one or multiple LED screens, capable of showing video or still-image advertisements or institutional messages. It’s a very creative and useful tool for out-of-home advertising.
Traditional billboards are large outdoor advertising boards that essentially remain bound to specific spots (normally highways and other high-traffic roads) to allure people to pay money for a product or service you’re offering.
Some more advanced trucks would have hydraulic stages and lifts incorporated to enable live performances, speeches, or product exhibitions as the ad is displayed (especially useful in the context of special events and fairs). Others would simply sport single or multiple LED screens, the latter enabling reproduction of multiple media files or visibility of the same advertising material from various angles.
Normally, for a marketing strategy to work, it would have to be directed towards people who fill our criteria of “ideal customers” or “buyer personas”, namely, the archetypes of a real person who would be more prone to spend money on our product or service.
Same with online marketing. While useful in some scenarios, most people would simply have to click the “skip ad” button or scroll away, leaving the rest of the advertisement largely unseen.
Another element to factor in is the attractiveness of mobile billboards. Since they’re not as common as other marketing mediums, they will ultimately provoke more attention from the audience.
Billboard spaces can be very onerous, ranging from 700-14,000$ per month. Meanwhile, as we’ll see shortly, mobile billboards can cost quite a lot more on rental (particularly if you plan to rent one for an entire month or year).
LED billboard trucks are naturally more expensive because of the technology employed to make them work. You will also have a limited allotted time to display the ad or message.
We would be tempted to say that it’s far more profitable to buy a billboard truck, especially if you plan on using it permanently for your advertising needs. Regardless, you ought to decide according to your marketing plan and projections.
