The aerator is a bit like a fine sieve, which separates a single stream of water into many small streams and surrounds them with air. This means that there is less space for the water to pass through, but the introduction of air into the mixture ensures that the water pressure does not drop significantly.
On the contrary, a faucet aerator can improve water flow and help it feel softer to the touch. By introducing small bubbles into the water, the faucet aerator can make the faucet run longer while using less water.
